# Go sources are checked out with LF endings regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# gofmt considers CRLF-terminated source unformatted. This repo is developed on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule git rewrites committed
# LF content to CRLF in the working tree and `gofmt -l .` reports every such
# file — a false positive against content that is already clean in the index,
# and one that made a local run disagree with CI's gofmt gate. Pinning the
# checkout is what makes the two agree. Committed bytes are unaffected.
*.go text eol=lf

# go.mod / go.sum are likewise tool-written and tool-read; keep them LF for the
# same reason.
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf
